# R47 Track B — PER-ARM POSITIVE CONTROL for the COMPENSATION that makes the
# adapter arms safe to convert.
#
# CELL: arm = combinator adapter, CLOSURE-STRUCT branch (`methods.rs`,
# `__Closure_N__call` inside `call_closure_in_adapter`) · combinator =
# `Option.unwrap_or_else` on the None path · payload = String.
#
# ⚠ THIS FIXTURE IS THE INSTRUMENT FOR THE RISKIEST HALF OF THE CHANGE. The
# adapter's `assign_result_local_move` performs a Move-mode assign WITHOUT
# zeroing the source, so `result_local` and the closure-call result end up
# holding the SAME pointer in TWO LIVE SLOTS — precisely the shape a
# self-nulling `free` cannot hide. Register the call result at birth and do
# nothing else, and both slots get released: double free.
#
# RED-VERIFIED, and not by a revert: with the register-at-birth conversion
# applied but the tracker-side transfer (`drops.unregister` of the moved-from
# source in `assign_result_local_move`) REMOVED, this program aborts under
# ASan with `attempting double-free`, 3/3 runs. It is CLEAN 3/3 at pristine
# `f3feea79` and CLEAN 3/3 with the full change — so it is neither a leak
# repro nor decoration: it pins the compensation exactly.
#
# INSTRUMENT: `security_safe_no_leak`, C lane only (ASan is a no-op under
# `--backend=llvm`). Fire count: 1 call at the adapter closure-struct arm.
String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Option[String] o = None()
    print(o.unwrap_or_else((): mk("hel", "lo")))
